<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Fine-tuning per Dataset</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ A.5 Fine-tuning per Dataset ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ In-Context Fine-Tuning for Time-Series Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, <a href="#A1.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ A.5 Fine-tuning per Dataset ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ In-Context Fine-Tuning for Time-Series Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and <a href="#A1.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ A.5 Fine-tuning per Dataset ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ In-Context Fine-Tuning for Time-Series Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> present the detailed accuracy and timing metrics to compare TimesFM-ICF and FT-TimesFM on Monash. While TimesFM-ICF is more accurate, it is also significantly faster than straighforward fine-tuning on the target dataset. Both are results of the TimesFM-ICF’s in-context learning capability.</p>
</div>
